# Spring Framework 6.2.19 is the latest 6.2.x release: both fixes ship only in 7.0.9, i.e. the Spring Boot 4
# major migration, which is out of scope (Renovate opens that upgrade). The samples only expose
# @RestController String endpoints, with no view technology and no Server-Sent Events, which both CVEs require:
#   CVE-2026-47884: XsltView behind a "/**" view-rendering mapping (RCE/SSRF)
#   CVE-2026-47890: stream corruption of SSE responses rendering view fragments
# Re-evaluate at expiry; drop the entries once Spring Boot 4 is adopted.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2026-11-09
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2026-11-09
